{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And he saw Amalek.</b> By way of prophecy, and the proverb: «the first of nations» — its meaning is that it is the nation that fights against Israel first, and its end is until it is destroyed. And so it was in the days of Saul, who killed from man to woman, from infant to suckling, and old man. And many interpreted «the first of nations» to mean that they are reckoned at the head of the nations, but this is not so."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:19:20.566311029Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}